/**
 * # Agricultural operations
 *
 * Sowing deliberately places seed into or onto a growing substrate. Germination
 * may follow, but seed placement does not guarantee it. Where germination is
 * observed as an event engendered by sowing, its instantiator model determines
 * whether it occurs in the particular conditions. Sowing can take place wherever
 * agricultural production is undertaken, with different means of placement and
 * at different scales.
 *
 * Spontaneous seed dispersal and seed storage are distinct from sowing, as is
 * transplanting an already growing plant. The crop being sown and any material
 * later harvested have their own identities. The act of sowing alone establishes
 * neither a cultivated individual nor a successful crop or harvest.
 */
ontology agriculture
    version 1.0
    using imod, physical, ecology
    in domain imod:Physical;

process Sowing
    "An agricultural activity deliberately placing seed into or onto a growing substrate."
    is physical:Activity;

/**
 * ## Water application and soil management
 *
 * Irrigation applies water for crop cultivation. Tillage mechanically disturbs
 * soil as an agricultural management activity. They describe deliberate
 * operations without selecting equipment, a spatial scale or a successful crop
 * outcome. Tillage involves soil; irrigation need not use soil as its substrate.
 *
 * Applying water is distinct from infiltration, uptake by an organism and
 * consumptive use. Tillage does not alone establish improved condition, a
 * particular disturbed-area fraction or a later yield. Observations identify
 * the operation and its participants; models describe the resulting water,
 * soil and biological changes.
 */
process Irrigation
    "Deliberate application of water for crop cultivation."
    is physical:Activity;

process Tillage
    "Mechanical disturbance of soil as an agricultural management activity."
    is physical:Activity;

/**
 * ## Experimental first-level articulation
 *
 * These observations extend the shared vocabulary for multidisciplinary review.
 * Their declaration-local review records preserve rationale, alternatives and
 * exact validation evidence. Experimental inclusion is distinct from recorded
 * community acceptance; models still establish occurrence, support and outcomes.
 */

@review(
    schema="klab.review/1",
    proposal="wv-review-20261023-0105",
    revision="strawman-integration-r1",
    maturity="experimental",
    controversy="unassessed",
    technical_validation="not_recorded",
    community_acceptance="not_recorded",
    review_record="../docs/reviews/domain-integration-20261023/records/living/agriculture.json"
)
process Transplanting
    "Deliberate placement of an already growing plant at a growing site."
    is physical:Activity;

